WEBVTT

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:08.300
Everyone's present is made possible by ghosts named the past.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.030
Because there is a present, there will be a future.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.610
The past is where the future begins.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.860
When ghosts pass on,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.870
I wonder if they become the nourishment for the future...

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.090
You can't run forever!

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.660
Don't you think you look bad doing this?

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.820
I can live with it.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.820
That's exactly what I mean when I say...

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.770
You don't look bad at all, Akito.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:08.980
Akito isn't a disgrace at all, not one bit!

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:13.110
As Captain, don't you think you should start being more concerned with the welfare of the Nadesico?

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:16.230
People don't live on the Nadesico alone!

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.530
I think you mean something completely different.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.270
Hey, you two, knock it off!

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.410
I have to object to how you're talking.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.080
You need to be more respectful of your Captain.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.240
Akatsuki! Don't make this any more complicated!

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.110
If you're not interested in the Captain,

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.600
well, then, I'll just have to take her off your hands.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.610
Of course you won't let something like that happen, right, Akito?

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.250
This is inappropriate on duty!

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:37.460
Hey. Do I detect a certain amount of jealousy from you, Erina-kun?

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:40.590
You...

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.050
You're going to crash.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.920
I have visual of the free-floating target.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.610
It's a miniature enemy shuttle. Starting retrieval procedure.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:04.700
Protect the "Visitor"?

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.620
I believe that the boson jump conducted was unstable,

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.290
and that made the shuttle suffer a stressful impact upon re-entry into normal space.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.920
Well, I just can't believe what a cute little girl like her would be doing out there all alone.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.460
We'll have to wait for her to regain consciousness.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.510
And I guess we didn't have to wait long for our princess.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:25.180
Where am I?

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.980
You're in the infirmary of the high mobile battleship Nadesico.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:29.810
Nadesico?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.450
Right.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.830
Are you okay? Does anything hurt?

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.220
Nadesico...

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:38.860
What is it?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.340
Who am I?

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.550
What am I doing here?

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.460
Let's see...

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.450
Your name is Shiratori Yukina.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:51.790
where you were unconscious after an accident.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.050
Oh, I hope you don't mind that your possessions were confiscated as part of security precautions.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.710
Oh no! Not that!

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.810
Regulations says I can't do something like that.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.700
But, that's a...

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.760
I sure a nice young lady such as yourself can understand...

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.800
In that case, you can keep this.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.770
So, you're suffering from memory loss, right?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:17.560
Yes.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.690
I see...

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:20.980
"Dash!"

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.150
I wonder if my cover's blown?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.180
Well, take care of yourself.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.040
Yukina...

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.360
I hope she doesn't do anything stupid or dangerous.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.500
Don't worry, justice always prevails at the end.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.910
Our goal is peace!

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.730
It's not a matter of who wins or loses!

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.670
I'm sure she's aware of that as well.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.960
Then why are you acting so anxious?

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.380
I believe in her...

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.180
Yes, I do.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.270
What do I care about peace?

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.710
Where are you, Haruka Minato?!

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.670
I'll never forgive you for stealing onii-chan's heart!

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.650
Nothing can stop me from finding her and beating her to a bloody pulp!

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.200
You took your time.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.480
What's wrong? Isn't this your room?

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:20.580
Why are you...

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.630
I'm chasing you because you're running away.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.030
Because you're running.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:25.980
I'm not running!

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:32.940
It's the pilot's duty to complete a mission report after returning to base. What can I do?

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.520
Is that the only reason why?

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.680
You're running, looking for a reason to run.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.140
Run from what?

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:41.480
I just don't want to believe that fighting is the right thing to do!

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:43.520
I'm not running away from you.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.470
Please leave. I'm going to get dressed and go to bed.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.910
I never said fighting is the right thing to do.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.500
You fight because the enemy attacks. What's wrong with that?!

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.450
That's not a reason I'm willing to accept.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.780
I'm going to take off my clothes.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:55.920
Why don't you?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.530
You need to face up to things you want to avoid...

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.670
I said, that's not good enough for me.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.250
Just give up fighting?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.110
People are going to die if you don't fight for them.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:10.950
What kind of a fool are you?

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.920
This is no time to hesitate.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:15.310
Any small child would understand what's at stake.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.980
Well, I don't. And neither am I hesitating!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.860
You need a reality check!

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.650
Whatever. I'm sick of fighting and experimenting.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.570
You're just like your father,
when he was working on the CCs...

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.180
What did you just say?

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:32.080
You know something, don't you?!

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.210
Don't close up to me with no clothes on, you Jofer!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.700
What's a "Jofer"?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.570
Baka...

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.990
You can't fight on an empty stomach.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.300
Her name was Yukina-chan?

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.250
I heard we got this new cutie in.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.950
She's a prisoner. POW.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.100
But she's cute, right?

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.120
She's only thirteen. A mere child.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.830
That kind of cute. I see.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.430
There, this is the girl.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:24.080
Hey, she is a cute one.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.170
Whoa...

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.590
I guess Earthlings know a thing or two about beauty after all.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.290
My niece is about her age.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.720
Suffering from memory loss, huh?

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.500
That's a shame.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:37.790
Too bad she can't get well and head home.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.770
Hopefully the war will be over by then.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.770
War stinks, man.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:42.920
That it does.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.980
I sure wish it would end soon.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:47.380
What is this?

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.730
Why are the evil, savage Earthlings talking like...

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:53.230
But wait. Maybe they already know I made a break for it,

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:55.780
and they're putting on this show to trick me so they can catch me.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:57.740
Yeah, that's gotta be it!

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:00.550
I have to hurry and find Haruka Minato.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:04.060
Men
Women
Nadesico Health Land

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.210
Are you going bathe now, Minato-san?

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:06.510
Men
Women
Nadesico Health Land

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:07.020
Yes.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.330
Men
Women
Nadesico Health Land

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.380
The bath was just right.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:11.880
Remember, hand on your hip.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.140
Okay.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.770
Oops, I forgot my shampoo.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.410
Haruka Minato.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.680
How dare you...

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:58.760
This is the ending theme to the manga that onii-chan loves...

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.180
Onii-chan...

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.610
There you are.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.060
Why do you know that song?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.490
Shiratori-san was nice enough to teach it to me.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.700
I like onii-chan, but...

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.660
I hate that manga.

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:20.820
You are brother and sister.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.370
You were planning to seduce onii-chan and then spy on us, weren't you?!

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.680
If I was, I'd have already have gone all the way with him.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.040
What do you mean, "gone all the way with him"?

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.710
It means I'd be a lot more intimate with him...

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.420
That's disgusting!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.630
Here I go again...

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.390
There you go again. Don't stand up all of a sudden...

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.130
Then tell me what's special about onii-chan.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.190
He has a wonderful younger sister like you.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:53.490
Don't play games with me!

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.420
I'm not playing games.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:58.240
You came all this way just because you were worried about him, right?

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.160
I think that's amazing.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:01.790
Well...

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.500
You see, I'm really happy...

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.290
To be able to meet you, so, please...

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.640
Don't do something like this.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.590
Were you planning on assassinating someone with this bomb?

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.550
That's wrong. Going on a suicide mission.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.970
Your brother would drown in sadness if you died.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:28.740
Will... Will you do it with onii-chan?

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:30.730
Do what?

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:31.510
Yes!

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:38.860
UEAF GHQ

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.400
Nadesico heading to Earth?
UEAF GHQ

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:42.470
Understood.

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:45.620
Yurika...

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:46.820
What?

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:02.650
This machine can be used for real-time communication?

00:11:02.650 --> 00:11:05.900
It's actually supposed to be used for peace negotiations.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.170
Wow, let me see. Let me see.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:29.440
What is it?

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.620
Yukina? Is this Yukina?!

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:34.040
Thank heavens. Are you alone, onii-chan?

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.960
Yes. But where are you right now?

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:39.390
Are you hurt? Is the ship intact?

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.420
I'm making an exception.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.050
It's been a long time.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.340
Yes, it has.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.380
You seem to be well...

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:51.800
Yes, I am.

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:54.070
Oh, man...

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:54.450
Yes?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.440
I don't know where to begin.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:59.070
No chitchat about that manga!

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.100
Baka! Why would I bring up something like that?!

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:04.610
She didn't tune in for toons.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.190
It's a pun...

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:12.660
Jovians make puns too.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:14.900
We Jovians are pretty jovial, you know.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:23.630
Too weak.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:25.260
Ouch, harsh.

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:28.680
Minato-san?

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.520
Huh? I wonder why? It's supposed to be funny...

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:38.520
Everyone, I would like to announce the decision I've made as captain.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.160
I believe we should protect our Shiratori Yukina-chan here,

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.950
and convince Nergal's leaders of the need to negotiate,

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:47.950
so that a peace treaty can become a reality.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:52.070
I don't think fighting is the only way to end a war.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:53.260
And more importantly,

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:55.710
I don't want to continue fighting with her homeland.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.040
Minato-san.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:58.710
Yes.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.880
Upon the day when a truce comes about...

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:02.140
Yes?

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.270
When peace does come, would you...

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.310
What's going on?

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:09.680
Yukina?

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.780
I don't know! I'm going to cut the transmission for now.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.100
What's the situation?

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.490
Multiple vessels are surrounding this ship.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:18.440
It appears to be a fleet.

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:22.170
Yugaoh... Harujyon... Mihejyon...

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.100
Why?

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.650
How have you been doing, Yurika?

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:27.950
Father!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:29.870
You've grown so...

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:33.330
Not just your breasts, of course.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:35.470
Father!

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:37.580
I'm talking about overall growth, of course.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:43.250
I've been instructed by Headquarters to insure the safety of Shiratori Yukina.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.820
Insure the safety?

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.760
The Nadesico already has Yukina-chan's safety well secured.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.670
I'm sorry, but you must hand her over immediately.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.590
What's going on? What happened?

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.390
You're being deceived, Tsukumo!

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.910
That woman is one of those evil, savage Earthlings!

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:00.980
What?

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.000
Return back to your old self.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:07.070
Recall those days when we worshipped Nanako-san as our most cherished presence.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.910
That woman is a mere stain on the floor compared to Nanako-san.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:10.780
You bastard!

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:15.330
Please tell us the reason.
Why is the Nadesico not sufficient?

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:19.730
Is there a place safer than inside of the most powerful warship ever?

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.880
I do not explain orders. They were given out from above.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.490
If you can't tell me a reason, then...

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.670
Prepare gravity blast cannon!

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.090
What?!

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:31.910
Shoot between the ships, please.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:33.010
Aye aye.

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:34.200
Wait a moment, Yurika!

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.890
Listen to what you father is trying to tell you.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:36.930
Fire!

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:38.600
Yurika!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.400
All systems down.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.500
You don't have to worry.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.660
The Nadesico won't crash just because I removed the master key.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.580
The system down process of gravitation control was deliberately made gradual.

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:00.620
We should safely land, or splash down.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:04.650
Why? I'm the only person that's supposed to be able to pull out that key.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.420
No, not quite. To be precise, you and one other.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.470
The chairman of Nergal.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:12.760
What does that mean?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.050
Come on. I'm that chairman.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.020
That's right. Were you surprised?

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:25.730
Baka...

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:28.390
Jeez, just like I thought.

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:29.560
Yeah, yeah. Whatever.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:32.110
This is just like Gekiganger.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.010
You knew all along?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.500
Clear as the sun in the cloudless sky,

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.860
former Heavyweight Champion Playboy, Akatsuki-san.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:40.040
Damn it! So what!

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:44.460
While this wasn't in my plans, from this instant on the Nadesico will be under my direct command.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.340
When you calm down and think about it,

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:50.300
having the military protect this young lady seems like a good idea.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:54.300
Oh, and if anyone doesn't agree, then they are welcome to get off the ship.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:56.890
Yukina-chan...

00:15:56.890 --> 00:16:00.060
Chairman Akatsuki, I myself will head over immediately.

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:03.390
Leave me to talk sense into Yurika and the others.

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:06.590
I believe there is no reason to further agitate matters.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:07.680
Seems fair.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.450
Don't worry. As your father, I will work all this out.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.660
What's happened to the girl from Jupiter?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.760
Would you like my help?

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.390
You don't look like you believe me.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:39.350
But I'm certain I would be more useful than your Captain.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.170
Maybe...

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.220
Then why?

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.640
I told you, I know about your father.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.090
Doesn't that intrigue you?

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:00.240
It seems even our associates don't trust us.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.500
You're becoming more like your father.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.670
What might you mean?

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.460
I'm just recalling days long past.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:20.600
Back when your father and Tenkawa-kun's parents participated in the discovery of the CCs.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:23.930
That day, just after the military was ordered to withdraw from Mars,

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.020
a coup d'etat took place.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:28.690
In all the confusion that followed, Akito's parents died.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:39.360
Nergal might have manipulated the parties involved in that affair.

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:41.180
Just as you are today.

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:43.290
What is this you are talking about?

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:45.290
I'm afraid I don't quite follow what you're saying.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:48.210
Then let me explore this subject a little further.

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:53.710
At the time, CCs were top secret.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.630
Nergal did not want to let anyone else know of their existence.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.550
But Professor Tenkawa was adamant on publicizing the findings.

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:02.470
And then the Professor and his wife died mysteriously.

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.390
Why bring this up now?

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.020
This probably is a good time to keep your mouth shut!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.380
I was the interim commander of the Mars branch office at the time.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:15.160
Looking back now, it all went unnaturally smoothly.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:17.650
Starting from when the military pulled out, the coup d'etat

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:21.330
and the abrupt containment of the confusion immediately following the deaths of the Professor.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:25.740
Suspecting something afoul, I accessed the corporate computer.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.660
Stop this. That's enough.

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:32.640
The leaders of Nergal decided that the Tenkawa couple must be assassinated.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:34.620
Akito...

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:39.300
It was all for the ruins discovered on Mars.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:45.940
The boson jump control mechanism left behind by ancient Martians or Jovians.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:48.920
It's a technology that will one day be capable of supporting the everyday life of mankind.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:52.400
My father saw what awaited the world, and planned accordingly,

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:55.350
consolidating under his ownership all interests that would be integral to the boson jump era.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:19:01.200
And so my father and mother were obstacles to those plans?!

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.370
What do you plan to do with that young girl?

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:05.780
The one named Shiratori Yukina?

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:08.880
The main Jovian fleet has already moved into Mars orbit.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:13.210
Any mention of peace negotiations made public will have an impact on the morale of the troops.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:15.630
In other words, she must be eliminated.

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:17.550
I suppose it will have to come to that.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.220
Of course, publicly, we will make it sound much less extreme.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.630
Well, I afraid it's come to this, everybody.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:24.780
Akito, run!

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.080
Don't go!

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:33.770
Stop this!

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:34.690
Damn...

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:38.720
Captain!

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:39.980
Yes!

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.790
Why don't you stop those experiments?

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.150
Do you still want to go on after what you just heard?

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:46.740
You must not go.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.090
I'm leaving.

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:48.570
No!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:49.490
I'm leaving.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:53.390
You can just go on with your life, where you do nothing but use people to get your way!

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:54.820
You can't go.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.660
Don't leave me!

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:04.180
I'm sorry.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:11.640
Freeze!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:13.690
Found them!

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:14.810
Damn it!

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:17.640
Out of the way!

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:24.360
Let's go!

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:27.910
Are you afraid?

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.890
I will protect her. No matter what!

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:39.670
Everybody run! Run!

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.280
Hello, Restaurant Yukitani here.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:51.450
You'll have the large ramen and fried rice with fried dumplings?

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:52.790
Right, one large, and fried rice with fried dumplings.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.930
And so, we took Yukina-chan with us as we ran out of the Nadesico, but...

00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:58.720
Stir fried vegetables, Chinese bowl and beef sauce lo mein order from front!

00:21:58.720 --> 00:21:59.140
All right!

00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:01.190
We can't let all this work bog us down.

00:22:01.190 --> 00:22:02.900
We have unfinished business to take care of...

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:05.110
Sato-san in Block Two's getting impatient for his ramen. Is it ready yet?

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:05.960
Yes, I just go it out!

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:08.020
So the next episode of Martian Successor Nadesico will be...

00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:09.420
"A Place We Call "Home!"

00:22:09.420 --> 00:22:10.750
Yes, it's all ready to go!

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:11.740
Eh?
